    <briefdescription>
<para>Standalone tamper-evident audit record writer with SHA-256 hash chain. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Each entry is stored as a JSON line with two extra fields injected: &quot;chain_seq&quot; — monotonically-increasing sequence number (uint64) &quot;prev_hash&quot; — SHA-256 hex digest of the previous log record&apos;s hash input</para>
<para>The running chain head is persisted to <computeroutput>chain_head_path</computeroutput> after every write so that <ref refid="classthemis_1_1utils_1_1_audit_log_verifier_1add5d810e8a6508bf8b83dc184efaa422" kindref="member">AuditLogVerifier::verify_chain()</ref> can verify from any checkpoint without replaying the whole log.</para>
<para>Initial chain seed: SHA-256 of a caller-supplied seed string (typically derived via HKDF from the cluster root key so chain heads are cluster-specific).</para>
<para>v1.5.0: Initial implementation (Phase 3 FUTURE_ENHANCEMENTS.md). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
